Review probes, round 2 (PR #314): six routes that still loaded node b
under Node 24 while the node was verified, now each unverified by the
allowlist (ADR 0025): module as a value with a bracketed "require" key,
the Function constructor through a "constructor" string key or a
destructured constructor key, process with computed keys, a sloppy
function's this passed to Reflect.get, and Annex B HTML-like comments
("<!--" anywhere, "-->" at a line start) that a template literal would
otherwise swallow. A TypeScript instantiation expression before "/" is
ambiguous. Controls: a JSON import with attributes, a .node addon, dlopen,
a computed tsconfig-alias import, a file using only the enumerated safe
forms (verified), and a declaration file, to which the allowlist does not
apply.
-- blok.json --
{"name":"shop","module":"example.com/shop","runtime":"go","layout":"unified","triggers":["http"],"types":""}
